                                "sense_id": "fc840a38-0c26-3c13-8631-a9cd7fc969e8",
                                "text": "In German, the ß character is called eszett. It’s used in “Straße,” the word for street, and in the expletive “Scheiße.” It’s often transliterated as “ss,” and strangely enough, it’s never had an official uppercase counterpart."
                            }
